# Experimental v1: visible portals to other maps and ordinary resources.
# In Zed, open this file, quickstart.lensmap and night-ferry.lensmap first.
# Map loading uses attached editor buffers, including unsaved edits.
version: v1
nodes:
  - id: notebook
    summary: A connected ferry notebook
    full_text: |
      # A connected ferry notebook

      Keep the small writing experiment, the larger ferry map and a few
      reference documents connected without copying them into one map.

      Click a portal to select it. Double-click, press Enter while the viewer
      or a thought has focus, or use its explicit Open action to enter it.
      Ordinary selection and Space do not open destinations.

      Open both destination maps in Zed before trying the map portals.
      Back returns to this notebook and its previous view.
    connections:
      # No fragment: enter the whole destination in fitted Overview.
      - type: map_link
        url: ./quickstart.lensmap
        summary: Try the quickstart
        full_text: |
          A small place to try Markdown thoughts, shared connections and cycles.
          Its source stays separate from this notebook.

      - type: map_link
        url: ./night-ferry.lensmap
        summary: Explore the night ferry
        full_text: |
          Open the complete ferry map in Overview, then choose a thought.

      # An authored thought ID is an exact target, not a generated heading slug.
      - type: map_link
        url: ./night-ferry.lensmap#tides
        summary: Jump to the tide window
        full_text: |
          Enter Lens view centred on the existing `tides` thought.
          This reaches the same destination map as the portal above,
          but starts at a particular thought instead of its Overview.

      - type: external_link
        url: https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/tides.html
        summary: What are tides?
        full_text: |
          Background reading from NOAA for the ferry's changing shoreline.
          This is an ordinary web resource, not another Lensmap document.

      # Minimal portal: without local prose, its address supplies the label.
      - type: external_link
        url: https://commonmark.org/help/

      # Relative file destinations are also external links, not map imports.
      - type: external_link
        url: ./README.md
        summary: Read the sample guide
        full_text: |
          Open the nearby Markdown guide through the editor's resource opener.
          A standalone browser cannot open local files; the viewer reports
          that limitation without replacing the current map.

      # Solid prevention connectors end in a blocking bar beside the outcome.
      - id: pier-closed
        summary: Pier closed for repairs
        full_text: |
          Suppose the boarding area and its shelter are both off limits.
          This event prevents the two possibilities below; the thoughts stay
          visible so we can plan around what is no longer available.

          Select this thought and explore its neighbourhood to inspect the
          blocking bars. They belong beside the affected thoughts, not in
          the middle of the lines. No simulation or automatic hiding occurs.
        connections:
          - type: prevents
            summary: Board at this pier
            full_text: Find another landing or postpone the crossing.
          - type: prevents
            summary: Use the pier shelter
            full_text: Arrange another dry place for passengers to wait.
